Z||000002||Old Lar||12-30-2001||10:27 PM||||Too late for any good advice.  When it comes to who makes the "better" parent it seems that the female always wins.  In NY one kid = 25% of your income, 2 kids = 40%.  2 kids by 2 different women = bankruptcy.<P>Just examples of what I have seen.  Skip out on the court ordered payments, garneshee wages or IRS goes after you.<P>No money for the mother = no money for a lawyer.<P>Unless you can prove gross maternal incomptance, you don't have a chance to get custody.  Then her mother would be able to get custody.<P>So get a good paying job, so you can get a good lawyer (if one exists)go for custody.  You will be paying for this child for the next 18 years, whether you are in his life or not.||||reg||9
Z||000003||Loki||12-30-2001||10:35 PM||||Im not worried about the money...And as far as  the money I already know how much that is in wyoming..no biggy, but its still a fight im gonna try.I have a good job, insuarance on him and everything, she cant support herslef and him on her own. an dill be damned h\if her mo0ther get gets custody, not after the life she gave the ex (throwing a kid throgh a wall isnt right) Im just asking Aaround till i can get the lawyer cuse i just dont know what to do anymore...<BR>thanx for the info<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">   <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000004||Her86GT||12-30-2001||10:38 PM||||I do know that she does not have a legal right to keep your son from you.  Unless she had some kind of proof that you were abusive or something (which from your story doesn't sound like it).  Even then, she would have to get a restraining order.  This all doesn't make any sense.  If you's split on normal terms, there is NO WAY that she can keep your son from you.  Besides, if you have nothing in writing, you's are still technically/legally together.  In a way, she is kidnapping your son because she does not have legal rights to do this.  Sounds like this child support payment is more of a ransom your ex is holding over your child's head.  Get the police involved if you have to.  Definitly get legal representation.  They will give you the best advice.  All I know is Canadian law but I'm sure the U.S. is somehow close in legal terms.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar2sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ejayerik||12-30-2001||10:51 PM||||I have a good buddy that is in the same situation. Everytime he calls to speak to his girl, the ex gets on the phone yelling.."Wheres my damn money?" His problem is that the DA isn't taking out as much as he should. In anycase, it shows(atleast on her behalf) where her mind is. You have every right to see your son. Unfourtunatly, she is in custidy of the child so the ball is in her court for now. Go to court and explain the situation. Don't be a smart-ass or try to destroy her charactor. It will only make things worse. If she has an attitude like that on the phone, she will most likely be like that in court. Be calm and collected and just explain the cercomstances. The judge has seen plenty of "he said she said" stuff. You should be fine.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Loki||12-30-2001||10:56 PM||||I really hope everything works..I|even if I don win custody All I care about is seeing my son, that means the most to me. And yes I know she is using him cause she hates me, we had a bad break up. Nothing physical, i nver did or would have hit her in anyway. We did argue but i thought it was from stress....who knows...Anyway thanx for letting me vent and hear from others..agian sorry for spelling i really think i broke something  hehe..<P>also goto my site <A HREF="http://www.fieroloki.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroloki.com</A>    you can tell I Love him from his link   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The video is cool if your on broadband<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">   <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||12.238.220.105||reg||1
Z||000007||California Kid||12-31-2001||12:30 AM||||You're in a real tough spot guy, but you already know that.<P>Based on what you've said above, the best way to set her in place is not to pay any support unless there is a court order to do so period!!! If she's the *****  you claim she is, she'll probably state she didn't get anything from you anyway. You need to have proof (receipts, cashed checks, etc) of any monies you have given her. You're only assurance is that the monies go through "The Friend of The Court" which keeps records on your payment.<P>You need a real good attorney and you have to remember not to call him on every little thing (most of these guys charge by the minute). The only person she is going to listen to is the court. If she's real bitter she probably won't listen to them until they threaten reversal of custody.<P>If you lost money on the airline ticket due to her temper, bring it to your attorneys attention.<P>It's not a fair system when it comes to matters like this, there is little you can do but play hard ball within legal limits.<P>Good Luck to you!! The best thing you can hope for is that she grows up soon and realizes she should act in the best interest of the child.||||reg||1
